<blockquote>
  <blockquote>
    <blockquote>
      <p align="center"><b><font color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial" size="7">Dreamweaver
      Rules of Conduct</font></b></p>
      <p align="center"><img border="0" src="newgalaxy9.jpg"></p>
      <p align="center"><u><b><font face="Arial" color="#F3DAE0" size="6"><img border="0" src="newgalaxy4.jpg" align="middle">Our
      'Virtues' are the Rules we Live By!<img border="0" src="newgalaxy4.jpg" align="middle"></font></b></u></p>
      <p><font face="Arial" size="5" color="#F3DAE0"><b><u>Courtesy:</u></b><font face="Arial">
 We expect all of our members to be respectful to
      others and never use profane language in /gu, /ooc or /shouts.&nbsp;We do not allow Kill Stealing, loot hogging, fights or obnoxious behavior
      in /gu, /ooc or /shouts.&nbsp;</font></font></p>
      <p><font face="Arial" size="5" color="#F3DAE0"><u><b>Honor:</b></u><font face="Arial">
      Our members are expected to be honorable in their dealings with others and always keep
      their word. We would like everyone we interact with to know we are
      a guild with high morals and standards of conduct. Never
      lie, cheat or seal! &nbsp;Dreamweavers will
      not allow members to take unfair advantage of other members nor outsiders.</font></font></p>
      <p><font face="Arial" size="5" color="#F3DAE0"><u><b>Strength:</b></u><font face="Arial">
      We need our members to <b>PARTICIPATE</b> in Events and Online in our Message Board Forums.
      Dreamweaver members should try to solve their own
      problems- before requesting guild assistance. </font>Always refrain from
      pestering or begging, regardless of the circumstances.</font></p>
      <p><font face="Arial" size="5" color="#F3DAE0"><u><b>Charity:</b></u><font face="Arial">
      We
      help those who help themselves...and other members. We expect our members
      to act in a way beneficial to all. Guild members are not required to help
      each other get loot, levels or items. If you are continually asking for help, expect to give help in return.</font></font></p>
      <p><font face="Arial" size="5" color="#F3DAE0"><b><u>Community:</u> </b>Dreamweavers
      is a Family. In raids and groups family always comes first! Seek out
      family groups before you join strangers and always greet and say goodbye
      to family if possible...regardless if it is in /gu or face to face. If you
      wish respect, you show respect.&nbsp;</font></p>
      <p><font face="Arial" size="5" color="#F3DAE0">After a new member has been
      in the guild for 30 days they can have their alternates invited and also
      sponsor prospective members.&nbsp;</font></p>
      <p align="center"><img border="0" src="newgalaxy9.jpg"></p>
      <p align="center"><u><b><font face="Arial" color="#F3DAE0" size="6"><img border="0" src="newgalaxy4.jpg" align="middle">General
      Rules<img border="0" src="newgalaxy4.jpg" align="middle"></font></b></u></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" face="Arial" color="#F3DAE0">1. Kill Stealing
      and Ninja Looting in not allowed in this guild.</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial">2. Never take
      over someone else's spawns (camps) without allowing them to kill the spawn
      first or without asking to share first.</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial">3. Using
      foul or abusive language in /gu, /ooc or /shout will not be tolerated.
      Neither
      will badmouthing guild members or other guilds.&nbsp;</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial">4. Do not scam
      other players to take their gear, platinum or items. I.E: like going LD holding the group's loot and not
      selling/splitting or Ninjalooting or running Casino's and not paying off
      the winner.&nbsp; &nbsp;</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" face="Arial" color="#F3DAE0">5. We do not
      allow begging or whining in guild say. Our members will not harass other
      members/players for power leveling or camping gear above their means.</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" face="Arial" color="#F3DAE0">6. If you have
      questions, concerns or trouble: Instead off&nbsp; discussing in guild say
      or the message boards, or before leaving the guild,&nbsp; Members <b> should</b> contact an
      officer online as soon as possible.</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font face="Arial" size="5" color="#F3DAE0">7</font><font face="Arial" size="5" color="#F3DAE0">.
      If a current member or officer of Dreamweaver removes themselves from the
      guild on purpose out of anger, hostility, etc. he/she must go through the
      application process again with all rules applying. Special exceptions to
      be made per an officer counseled, case-by-case review.</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" face="Arial" color="#F3DAE0">8. If your Main
      leaves less than honorably, you must also remove your alternate characters
      or an officer will remove them. </font><font face="Arial" color="#F3DAE0" size="2">(This
      rule was made effective May 20, 2003.)&nbsp;</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font face="Arial" size="5" color="#F3DAE0">9. If you are
      going to sell your account on Ebay or give it away/trade it, please remove
      your characters from the guild. If you don't, the officers will once we
      find out someone else is playing using that account.</font></p>
      <p align="center"><img border="0" src="newgalaxy9.jpg"></p>
      <p align="center"><font color="#F3DAE0" size="5" face="Arial">&nbsp;</font><u><b><font face="Arial" color="#F3DAE0" size="6"><img border="0" src="newgalaxy4.jpg" align="middle"></font></b></u><font face="Arial" color="#F3DAE0" size="6"><b><u>Raiding
      Rules</u></b></font><u><b><font face="Arial" color="#F3DAE0" size="6"><img border="0" src="newgalaxy4.jpg" align="middle"></font></b></u></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial">Raids are established
      for a purpose... usually experience/gear or for Quest Items. Know why you
      are on the raid!</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial">Raids will be shown
      on Calendar, Announced in Weekly Newsletters, Posted on the Message Boards
      and Posted in the Guild M.O.T.D!</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial">If you wish to join a
      certain raid, make sure you are on site <b>BEFORE</b> the raid is scheduled to
      begin. </font></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial">Listen to your Raid
      Leader in the Channel He or She has set up! The Raid Leader has last say
      over how the raid is to be held. </font></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial">The Raid Leader will
      not only assign members to groups, and the Group Leader, but also list
      rules for that raid and how loot will be divvied up!</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial">The Group Leader
      should keep track of their members and if there are concerns about XP or
      Loot etc., members should ask the Group Leader - who <b> IN TURN</b> will ask the
      Raid Leader.</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font face="Arial" size="5" color="#F3DAE0">Raid leaders will
      choose Guild members over other characters wanting to join the raid.</font></p>
      <p align="center"><img border="0" src="newgalaxy9.jpg"></p>
      <p align="center"><u><b><font face="Arial" color="#F3DAE0" size="6"><img border="0" src="newgalaxy4.jpg" align="middle"></font></b></u><font face="Arial" color="#F3DAE0" size="6"><b><u>Loot
      Rules</u></b></font><u><b><font face="Arial" color="#F3DAE0" size="6"><img border="0" src="newgalaxy4.jpg" align="middle"></font></b></u></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial">This Guild operates on
      a NEED before GREED
      basis!&nbsp; </font></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial">
      <b><u>FINAL DECISIONS:</u></b> will be made by a Loot Council Comprised of Raid
      Leader, Officers and 2 Non Officers on the Raid.&nbsp;</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial"><b><u>Bp/Legs or Rare:</u></b>
      are awarded to Senior Member if the gear is an UPGRADE and WILL BE USED!
      Replaced Item should be handed down when Possible!</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial"><b><u>Normal Loot Items:</u></b>
      should be given to the player class that can use it. If more
      than one member has the same class, it's rolled for.&nbsp;</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font color="#F3DAE0"><font size="5" face="Arial">In the case of
      duplicate items being dropped/multiple items of that class: the person who has one already,
      or has won loot already,&nbsp; is exempt
      from rolling on it again until everyone has had a chance and/or received
      loot.&nbsp;</font></font></p>
      <p align="left"><font color="#F3DAE0"><font size="5" face="Arial">If all members can
      use it: the item is then rolled for at then end of that raid.&nbsp; You
      have to stay in the raid if you want loot at the end of it!</font></font></p>
      <p align="left"><font color="#F3DAE0"><font size="5" face="Arial">If the item is No
      Drop: it's rolled for before decay - by members who can use it with the
      character at the raid.&nbsp;</font></font></p>
      <p align="left"><font size="5" color="#F3DAE0" face="Arial">Loot that
      is for an EPIC or QUEST that a member is doing is exempt.&nbsp;</font></p>
      <p align="left"><font color="#F3DAE0"><font size="5" face="Arial">Ninja Looting is not
      tolerated nor honorable.&nbsp; We want all of our members to
      prosper, but not at the sake of depriving other members.</font></font></p>
      <p align="center"><img border="0" src="newgalaxy9.jpg"></p>
      <p align="center"><font face="Arial" color="#F3DAE0" size="3"><b>Updated:
      October 2003</b></font></p>
    </blockquote>
  </blockquote>
</blockquote>

